        "exposure_window_count": 1
      },
      "remediation": {
        "description": "Principal has an Auto Scaling–mediated escalation path. Its iam:PassRole grant reaches a role whose effective permissions exceed the principal's own, and its autoscaling grants allow it to create a launch configuration and auto scaling group that indirectly launch an EC2 instance with that role as the instance profile. The instance's user-data or shell can read IMDS credentials for the role and perform any action the role is authorised for.",
        "action": "Scope iam:PassRole to a role whose effective permissions do not exceed the principal's, or remove autoscaling:CreateLaunchConfiguration and autoscaling:CreateAutoScalingGroup. If auto scaling capability is required, enforce an instance-profile allowlist via a Condition on iam:PassRole (Condition.StringEquals: iam:PassedToService == ec2.amazonaws.com together with a narrowly-scoped Resource ARN).",
        "example": "{\n  \"identity\": {\n    \"kind\": \"user\",\n    \"escalation\": {\n      \"passrole_autoscaling\": {\n        \"present\": false\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n"
      },
